## Lore

The seljuk came off Gemini One, a planet where dinosaurs were the dominant life
form - and the archaeological record shows those dinosaurs were identical to
Earth''s, from the Jurassic and the Cretaceous. Parallel evolution or Rift
activity; nobody knows.

About fifty million years ago a powerful P.P.E. storm irradiated the planet,
probably out of a mega-Rift opening on Gemini''s twin. Every life form larger
than a mouse turned supernatural and mega-damage. The species that were not
affected died out, unable to compete with things that were effectively
invulnerable, and freak hurricanes and ley line storms kept depositing
supernatural predators on top of that.

What came out of it descended from the planet''s top predator, Tyrannosaurus Rex.
One branch became the dreaded Terror Lizard. Another became smaller and smarter -
a fast pack hunter with long, dexterous hands - and that branch became the
seljuk.

## The day magic ended

The seljuk did something no other magic-using race has. Soon after their first
cities, a circle of powerful magicians set out to protect the planet from the
ley line storms that could destroy in minutes what had taken generations to
build. In a ceremony still honoured in seljuk religious gatherings, they turned
the planet''s own P.P.E. against itself and sealed it against Rift and ley line
activity.

The price was permanent and everyone paid it. Only the sacrifice of every
person''s P.P.E. capacity could power the ritual, and the day the Rifts were
banished was the last day any seljuk worked magic. A race that might have been
among the great sorcerers of the Megaverse gave it up entirely.

The tales say even that ritual would have failed without the Cosmic Forge: the
sorcerers conducting it received a communication at the crucial moment and found
their power doubling just long enough to finish. All of them glimpsed the Forge,
and it has been central to most seljuk religion ever since.

## Chivalry

The end of the Time of Chaos let the seljuk turn their predatory instincts on
the hunt for knowledge. The culture that eventually won out was one of defending
warriors - fighters who held it a duty and a privilege to protect the weak, and
who saw war as a necessary evil - and it united the planet under a Protectorate
with a parliamentary government.

Noro explorers made first contact, were intimidated, and found the seljuk
honorable and reasonable and eager to learn. Trade followed, then the gravity
drive, then colonies. When the Kreeghor Empire began encroaching, the seljuk
knew they could not fight it alone - many of their planets had already
surrendered rather than be obliterated - and, like the wolfen before them, they
asked the CCW for help and joined.

Honor and courage are respected above all else, and renegades who break the code
are exiled or executed depending on what they did. For a seljuk to fully respect
someone, that person must show bravery and conviction - not brute strength and
not bravado. A person who stands up for what they believe is a hero in seljuk
eyes.

## GM Notes

A seljuk can take most O.C.C.s, Consortium and Empire ones alike, and can even
be a psychic R.C.C. like a mind melter or a burster - but never a psi-stalker.
The one hard limit is magic: no magical O.C.C. is available to this race, ever.

For experience, the book says to use the seljuk R.C.C. table or the O.C.C.''s,
whichever is higher. The app cannot compare them, so the race carries no table
and the O.C.C.''s applies; the seljuk ladder is written out in the extraction
notes for a GM who wants to check.

They get on very well with most Consortium races, and those inside the Empire
have the respect of the kreeghor.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'seljuk');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'seljuk';

